Subject: [PATCH] partition: report the Next state after loading the choice page

ChoicePage::init() applies initialPartitioningChoice and emits
nextStatusChanged before PartitionViewStep::continueLoading() connects
to it. The step keeps reporting Next as disabled from the time the
waiting widget was shown, and ChoicePage only emits again when its
state changes. With a preset choice, Next stays disabled until the
user picks another choice, and autoProceed never proceeds.

Emit the current state once after connecting.
---
--- a/src/modules/partition/PartitionViewStep.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/partition/PartitionViewStep.cpp
@@ -100,6 +100,12 @@
 
     connect( m_core, &PartitionCoreModule::hasRootMountPointChanged, this, &PartitionViewStep::nextPossiblyChanged );
     connect( m_choicePage, &ChoicePage::nextStatusChanged, this, &PartitionViewStep::nextPossiblyChanged );
+
+    // ChoicePage::init() already applied the initial partitioning choice and
+    // emitted nextStatusChanged before the connection above existed. Report
+    // the current state now, otherwise Next stays disabled until the user
+    // changes the choice, and autoProceed never proceeds.
+    nextPossiblyChanged( true );
 }
 
 PartitionViewStep::~PartitionViewStep()
